1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,320
‘Life is for living’, according to the well-used expression: What we choose to do is up to us.
有句老生常谈的话是这么说的：“人生在世，就要活出精彩”。我们选择过怎样的生活，全凭自己做主。

2
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:16,920
That may not be completely true, but there is no harm in dreaming about what we’d like to achieve in our life.
这话或许并非完全正确，但畅想一下自己毕生想要实现的目标，总归是无伤大雅的。

3
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:24,740
Many of us write a list of things we’d like to do before we die – often called a bucket list.
很多人都会写下一份“人生愿望清单”，罗列自己离世前想做的事。

4
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:36,280
Bucket lists have been called ‘the greatest hits of your life’ and have helped some people overcome anxiety which would have stopped them following their dreams.
人生愿望清单被称为“人生中的高光时刻清单”，它帮助一些人克服了阻碍他们追逐梦想的焦虑情绪。

5
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:48,620
Some of us may choose to write one to fill our life with exciting and new experiences – from skydiving to swimming with sharks – the list is unlimited.
有些人会选择列这样一份清单，让生活充满新奇刺激的体验——从高空跳伞到和鲨鱼同游，清单上的内容可以无穷无尽。

6
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:54,820
This is something the BBC radio programme All In The Mind has been looking at.
英国广播公司电台节目《心灵深处》就探讨过这个话题。

7
00:00:54,820 --> 00:01:07,080
It heard from a blogger called Annette White who said she made a promise to live her bucket list which “continuously pushes the comfort zone to its limits and beyond it.”
节目采访了博主安妮特·怀特，她表示自己下定决心要完成人生愿望清单，这份清单“不断将舒适区推向极限，甚至突破极限”。

8
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:14,380
Such a list can be exciting and can indeed help you plan your life and give you focus.
这样的清单能让人满怀期待，也确实能帮你规划人生、明确方向。

9
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:32,380
When the BBC reporter Helen Fawkes knew she was suffering from incurable ovarian cancer, she took comfort in drawing up a bucket list - although she called it her ‘list for living’ because these were things for making the most of life.
英国广播公司记者海伦·福克斯在得知自己患上了无法治愈的卵巢癌后，从拟定人生愿望清单这件事里获得了慰藉——不过她把这份清单称为“人生清单”，因为清单上的事情都是为了充分享受生活。

10
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:41,030
Sadly, she was not able to achieve all of her 50 things before she died at the age of 45.
令人惋惜的是，在她45岁离世前，没能完成清单上的全部50件事。

11
00:01:41,030 --> 00:01:56,530
Creating a bucket list can certainly give us hope, but some people have argued it can be used as a coping strategy to try to control something uncontrollable – death.
拟定人生愿望清单固然能给我们带来希望，但也有人认为，这不过是一种应对策略，试图去掌控一些无法掌控的东西——比如死亡。

12
00:01:56,530 --> 00:02:07,930
Clinical psychologist Linda Blair told the BBC that she was “not really in favour of bucket lists… [they] take you away from the chance to be spontaneous.”
临床心理学家琳达·布莱尔在接受英国广播公司采访时表示，她“并不太赞成人生愿望清单……这类清单会让你错失随性而为的机会”。

13
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:15,430
It’s probably true that a list can encourage people to follow someone else’s idea of the perfect life.
确实，清单可能会促使人们去追逐别人眼中的完美人生。

14
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:28,880
And also, following a fixed list of goals makes you less impulsive - your aims and wishes might change as you approach the day when you finally kick the bucket.
而且，照着一份固定的目标清单行事，会让你变得不再随性——当你离人生终点越来越近时，你的目标和心愿或许也会随之改变。

15
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:33,320
But why not at least dream of what we would like to do?
但我们至少可以畅想一下自己想做的事，不是吗？

16
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:38,340
Why not reach for the stars, even if we only reach the sky?
为什么不心怀高远、奋力追梦呢？即便最终没能实现目标，至少也努力过。

17
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:48,280
Whether we want to plan it or just see what happens, we don’t know what tomorrow will bring, so maybe we should live for today.
无论我们是想规划人生，还是选择顺其自然，都要知道，未来充满未知，或许我们应该活在当下。
